From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:54:16 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 29/45] inkling2: decode-width mix stages slices; wide calls
 keep the old kernel

The register version still waited on its loads one after another. The
decode-width kernel now copies 2,048-column slices of every block into
shared memory with asynchronous 16-byte copies and sums from there:
34.6 vs 42.4 us at one row and 39 vs 66 us for three queries, but slower
at 64 rows, so calls over 16 rows run the original kernel. Both add the
same values in the same order: equal bits (checksums equal at 1-64 rows).
---
